{"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batch"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AsyncSequences"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent14AsyncSequencesO5BatchV","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsyncSequences\/Batch","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Batch"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent13BatchStrategyP","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchStrategy"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sci7ElementQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Strategy"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Afluent13BatchStrategyP7ElementQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When to emit the gathered elements; its ","type":"text"},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is this","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence’s, inferred from the call.","type":"text"}]}],"name":"strategy"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A sequence of the upstream’s elements, in order, in arrays of one or more.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The strategy decides when the pending elements are flushed: every so many elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/count(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":"), every interval","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/time(interval:clock:tolerance:)","type":"reference"},{"text":"), on a signal or a unit of work","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy","type":"reference"},{"text":"), whenever any of several does","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/either(_:_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":"), or by a rule of your own (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy","type":"reference"},{"text":"). After every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"flush, each strategy starts over. A flush with nothing pending emits nothing; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence never emits an empty array.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the upstream finishes, the pending elements, if any, are emitted as a last array and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the sequence finishes. When the upstream throws, the pending elements are dropped and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sequence throws the same error. A signal that finishes stops firing while the batches go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on; a signal that throws ends the sequence with its error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream and the strategy run in tasks of their own, started when iteration begins,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and arrays the consumer hasn’t taken yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are buffered. Cancelling the consumer, or dropping its iterator, cancels both. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"upstream or signal that ignores cancellation keeps the internal task alive until its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pending "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns, and is not read again after that; the batched sequence itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends at once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Batching needs iOS 16, Mac Catalyst 16, macOS 13, tvOS 16, watchOS 9 or visionOS 1.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Example","level":2,"anchor":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["for try await batch in [1, 2, 3, 4].async.batch(strategy: .either(.count(3), .time(interval: .seconds(1), clock: ContinuousClock()))) {","    print(batch) \/\/ Prints [1, 2, 3], then [4]","}"]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Throws","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any error the upstream or the strategy throws.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsynchronousUnitOfWorkSequence"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gathers elements into arrays and emits each array when the strategy says to flush."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/AsynchronousUnitOfWorkSequence\/batch(strategy:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/asynchronousunitofworksequence\/batch(strategy:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","extendedModule":"_Concurrency","modules":[{"relatedModules":["_Concurrency"],"name":"Afluent"}],"platforms":[{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"16.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"16.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"16.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"13.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"16.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"visionOS","introducedAt":"1.0"},{"beta":false,"unavailable":false,"deprecated":false,"name":"watchOS","introducedAt":"9.0"}],"role":"symbol","title":"batch(strategy:)","externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE5batch8strategyAA14AsyncSequencesO5BatchVy_xqd__Gqd___tAA0H8StrategyRd__ACQyd__ADRSlF::SYNTHESIZED::s:7Afluent30AsynchronousUnitOfWorkSequenceV","conformance":{"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Element","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},"fragments